# A finite incompatibility-to-log criterion with the extensive cost retained

Parent unreviewed deduction,31October2026, outside assessment1592. The abstract activity bound is the exact two-note conditional result assessed there; the induction below is NEW parent reasoning and inherits no assessment. This is a finite hard-core gas statement, not a new paper or a novelty claim.

## Precise finite criterion

Let P be a finite set of polymer TYPES with a symmetric REFLEXIVE incompatibility relation. For Gamma subset P define Z_Gamma(w) as the sum over compatible subsets of Gamma of the product of their complex activities w_gamma; the empty family contributes1. Fix nonnegative majorants rho_gamma and a_gamma. Put mu_gamma=rho_gamma exp(a_gamma). Assume, INCLUDING the self term,

    sum_(delta incompatible with gamma) mu_delta <= a_gamma.

Then throughout |w_gamma|<=rho_gamma, every finite Z_Gamma is nonzero, and for gamma in Gamma the ratio Z_Gamma/Z_(Gamma without gamma) lies in the disk centered at1 of radius at most1-exp(-mu_gamma). It has the principal logarithm with

    |Log[Z_Gamma/Z_(Gamma without gamma)]| <= mu_gamma.

The analytic logarithms on the polydisc interior are chosen to vanish at zero activities. Closed-polydisc inequalities follow as well from the strict positive disk margin. Majorants and mu are fixed for the entire domain; they are not chosen separately for each value of w.

## Induction, including the nonzero margin

Induct on the number of allowed types. The empty gas has Z=1. For gamma in Gamma let W=Gamma without gamma and let N be its types incompatible with gamma. The EXACT recursion is

    Z_Gamma = Z_W + w_gamma Z_(W without N).

All partition functions on the right involve proper subsets. Remove the types of N from W one at a time. The inductive lower bounds on the corresponding ratios yield

    |Z_(W without N)/Z_W| <= exp(sum_(delta in N) mu_delta).

Therefore the error q=Z_Gamma/Z_W-1 satisfies

    |q| <= rho_gamma exp(sum_(delta in N) mu_delta)
         <= rho_gamma exp(a_gamma-mu_gamma)
          = mu_gamma exp(-mu_gamma)
         <= 1-exp(-mu_gamma) < 1.

The penultimate inequality is equivalent to 1+mu<=exp(mu). Self-incompatibility is what supplies the subtracted mu_gamma. For mu_gamma=0, rho_gamma=0 and q=0. The disk avoids zero. The convergent scalar Log(1+q) series gives |Log(1+q)|<=-log(1-|q|)<=mu_gamma. This proves the induction for every gamma and Gamma, without assuming the desired connected expansion or any volume-independent lower bound on Z.

For any subset X of deleted types, telescoping these analytic logarithms gives

    |log Z_Gamma-log Z_(Gamma without X)| <= sum_(gamma in Gamma intersect X) mu_gamma.

There is no branch ambiguity: each ratio stays in the disk at1, the finite product telescopes, and every logarithm vanishes at w=0. In particular |log Z_Gamma|<=sum_(gamma in Gamma)mu_gamma and exp(-sum mu)<=|Z_Gamma|<=exp(sum mu). These costs can be extensive.

## Apply only to the EXACT finite activity gas1574

Take the original-label activities z(S) from1574/1592, compatibility meaning disjoint RAW scalar supports. Nonempty S is incompatible with itself. Let |S| be the number of original labels, and assume the stated original support-overlap maximum degree Delta. For a chosen eta>0 set a_S=eta|S| and majorant rho_S=|z(S)|. Let

    lambda_eta=lambda exp(eta), A=e sqrt(6),
    R=max(1,Delta+2BDmJ),
    b_eta=lambda_eta-lambda_eta A log(1-lambda_eta A R).

The assessed1592rooted estimate gives sup_r sum_(S contains r)|z(S)|exp(eta|S|)<=b_eta whenever lambda_eta A R<1, under all its uniform hypotheses. The incompatibility union bound in the actual1592report yields

    sum_(S incompatible with T) rho_S exp(eta|S|)
      <= (Delta+1)|T| b_eta.

Thus the explicit sufficient condition (Delta+1)b_eta<=eta supplies the finite criterion above. No component factorial or Mayer-family factorial is borrowed. Combined interaction-plus-cutoff-tail incidence and the original all-subsets product bound remain required.

An entirely explicit, loose smallness window follows from lambda_eta A R<=1/2: b_eta<=lambda_eta(1+A log2). It is enough to require both

    lambda exp(eta) <= 1/(2 A R),
    lambda exp(eta) <= eta/[(Delta+1)(1+A log2)].

This is an abstract sufficient window in declared constants, not a verified regime for the physical source. It fails to give an application if the actual constants grow with coupling/scale faster than the claimed small parameter decreases.

For the finite original label universe I, sum_S mu_S<=|I|b_eta by summing over roots (a harmless overcount by |S|). Hence |log Z|<=|I|b_eta and |1/Z|<=exp(|I|b_eta). A VOLUME-INDEPENDENT reciprocal is not concluded. If X consists of all polymer types incompatible with an original test-label set A0, the gas-deletion logarithm costs at most (Delta+1)|A0|b_eta. This is deletion in an abstract gas, not a physical conditional measure, changed cutoff or locality theorem for actual source observables.

For auxiliary original-label activities u_i, exact multilinearity of the finite factor expansion gives weights w_S=z(S)product_(i in S)u_i. A uniform |u_i|<=u0 uses lambda replaced by u0 lambda in the same conditions, giving a genuine auxiliary-activity zero-free polydisc. These u_i are not the source's complex background/current variables or moving domains. Analyticity/Taylor convergence of a finite log on this polydisc does not by itself prove absolute Mayer cluster coefficient bounds, spatial clustering, a thermodynamic limit, normalized marginal transport or an intrinsic counterterm identity.

## Provenance and finite checks

The classical bibliographic antecedent is [Kotecky and Preiss, Cluster expansion for abstract polymer models, CMP103,491–498(1986), DOI10.1007/BF01211762](https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211762). Its metadata was inventoried, not its original theorem/proof read or audited here. The search-indexed UCLA PDF returned404 through the browser tool; the author's2006exposition URL timed out there. Those access outcomes are retained; no quoted or unseen source proof is asserted. The complete finite induction above stands as own conditional reasoning and makes no novelty claim.

The attached exact rational-complex calculation checks partition recursion and deletion ratios on all64subsets of six overlapping polymer types. It also checks the failure of omitting self-incompatibility (one type of weight-1 has zero partition function), and the extensive independent-cutoff example. These are finite checks, not a proof of the universal theorem or source admission.

Mechanism: use the self term in the incompatibility budget to keep every finite deletion ratio away from zero, then telescope the correctly chosen logarithms. Hypothesis reduction: conditional abstract finite zero-free/logarithm control from the already stated rooted activity norm; no uniform normalizer claim. Levels: literature—classical bibliographic metadata only for this new citation; formal—no Lean proof or build; analytic conditional deduction—own new finite induction, unreviewed; heuristic—actual source instantiation; speculative—full physical normalization/marginal/complex-background conclusion. Falsifiers: omitted self term, incorrect activity/incompatibility dictionary, lost combined-label incidence, or an uncontrolled uniform-constant regime. Keep all1592source/geometry/row-sum objections. Do not publish this as assessed1592 or as a separate minor paper.
